From: Qiang Ma <maqianga@uniontech.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 20:46:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] LoongArch: KVM: Check the return values for put_user()
References: bsc#1012628
Patch-mainline: 7.1.5
Git-commit: fb89e0fe2dc4246c86ad0eb0fa2b7cb2f8ba9728

commit fb89e0fe2dc4246c86ad0eb0fa2b7cb2f8ba9728 upstream.

put_user() may return -EFAULT, so, when the user space address is
invalid, the caller should return -EFAULT.

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reviewed-by: Bibo Mao <maobibo@loongson.cn>
Signed-off-by: Qiang Ma <maqianga@uniontech.com>
Signed-off-by: Huacai Chen <chenhuacai@loongson.cn>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Slaby <jslaby@suse.cz>
---
 arch/loongarch/kvm/vcpu.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/loongarch/kvm/vcpu.c b/arch/loongarch/kvm/vcpu.c
index 4c6e2c05daaf..8101ecad02cf 100644
--- a/arch/loongarch/kvm/vcpu.c
+++ b/arch/loongarch/kvm/vcpu.c
@@ -1108,7 +1108,8 @@ static int kvm_loongarch_cpucfg_get_attr(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu,
 		return -ENXIO;
 	}
 
-	put_user(val, uaddr);
+	if (put_user(val, uaddr))
+		return -EFAULT;
 
 	return ret;
 }
-- 
2.55.0

